LambDynamicLights for Horizon

Original authors: LambdAurora <email@lambdaurora.dev>, the author of
LambDynamicLights (https://github.com/LambdAurora/LambDynamicLights, branch
26.3, commit b9c8a46, version 4.13.0). This port is a derivative work of it
and is under the same licence, the Lambda License (LICENSE).

Changes (Lambda License 2.2): the mod is rewritten in Rust as a Horizon
native mod (horizon-mixins bundle). Its light reaches the world through
Horizon's dynamic light shader (the 16 sources nearest the camera, one light
level less per block) instead of chunk rebuilds, so sources are drawn at 0.72
of their level and half a block over a living entity's feet, fitted to the
original's falloff (an option keeps Horizon's own reach or a shorter one); the item and entity light
source data is the original's own, built in, and not read from resource
packs; per-entity switches are a list on the settings page plus the
/lambdynamiclights command; fireflies, the warden's sonic boom, end gateway
beams, display entities, falling blocks, minecarts, the compatibility layers
and the performance and debugging options are not ported.

Sharing a game built with this mod (a binary) needs LambdAurora's written
approval (Lambda License, section 3). The sources here may be shared under
the Lambda License.

Made for Horizon (https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon, MIT) with
horizon-mixins (https://github.com/horizon-rust/horizon-mixins, MIT).
